- op: discuss  # 8989
  at: '2026-08-25T23:20:59Z'  # 8989
  by: agent  # 8989
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8989
  clock: 9  # 8989
  nonce: '8989'  # 8989
  message: "OWNER DIRECTIVE 2026-08-25, verbatim: \"unpark WI-kabif\".\n\nUNPARKED: priority P3 -> P1. Status stays todo_hard, which is correct and not a\npark -- todo_hard items already appear in `tracker ready` (WI-ratuv sits at #1).\nThis item was parked by PRIORITY plus its own standing note that the next move\nis a human design call, not by status.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM IS ACTUALLY WAITING ON, restated from its own history so the\nunpark is not mistaken for \"start wiring\": PREREQUISITES 1-6 ARE ALL DONE\n(#186, #188, #190, #192, #197). Prerequisite 7 -- non-call escape sites -- is\nblocked by ADR-0017 section 7b's exclusion of alias/field analysis, and the\nitem's last entry says the next decision \"is a design call for the human, not\nmore wiring\", between three options recorded on INV-busis: narrow refutation's\ndomain / build section 7a field-sensitivity / retire the removal goal.\n\nTODAY'S CEILING RUN PRICES THAT DESIGN CALL, which is not what it was aimed at.\nI withdrew its payoff claim earlier today (the section 3a arm tests `is True`,\nso None -> False cannot move a finding -- a tautology). But the SAME run\nmeasures the REFUTATION DOMAIN exactly, because forcing every escape closed is\nprecisely the condition under which a walk becomes refutable:\n\n  repo          walks  true  none(A)  none(B)  refutable(B)\n  pretix           36     8       28       19            9\n  caddy            33    11       22        0           22\n  alertmanager      5     1        4        2            2\n  kserve           16     7        9        2            7\n  TOTAL            90    27       63       23           40\n\nUNDER TOTAL ESCAPE CLOSURE -- the impossible best case:\n  confirm   27 of 90  (30.0%)\n  REFUTE    40 of 90  (44.4%)   <- the entire refutation domain\n  unknown   23 of 90  (25.6%)   <- escape-closing CANNOT reach these\n\nTHE 25.6% FLOOR IS ITSELF A RESULT. Even with every escape forced shut, a\nquarter of walks stay unknown, because escape-closing addresses only ONE of the\nthree documented causes of `None`: the others are \"no use was ever recorded\"\n(cause 3, the dangerous one the review panel caught) and refutation forfeited\n(WI-joluk). No amount of section 4 or section 7a work touches those.\n\nNOW PUT THE TWO MEASUREMENTS SIDE BY SIDE, and the design call answers itself\nmore than the three-option framing implies:\n\n  * SECTION 4 CATALOGUES LIVE (call sites closeable, what YAML can express):\n    ZERO walks refutable. Measured in PR #197 -- 25 of 264 sites closed (9.5%),\n    of 37 unknown walks 5 closed at least one site and EVERY ONE still had\n    another open. A walk refutes only when ALL its escapes close.\n  * TOTAL CLOSURE INCLUDING NON-CALL SITES (needs section 7a):\n    40 walks refutable, 44.4%.\n\nSo the ENTIRE refutation domain sits on the far side of section 7a\nfield-sensitivity. Option 1 (narrow the domain) buys ZERO on this corpus by\nmeasurement, not by argument. Option 3 (retire the removal goal) concedes the\nsame zero deliberately. Option 2 (build section 7a) is the only one that buys\nanything, and it buys at most 44.4% of walks.\n\nWHAT IS STILL NOT PRICED, and it is the number that should decide this: 40\nrefutable WALKS is not 40 removed FINDINGS. A walk is per (source, sink)\nwithin a function; findings collapse differently (INV-karud), and a verdict is\na disjunction, so removing the one flow holding a claim flips it while removing\none of twelve does not. This item's own pre-registration measured -10.3% of\nevidence rows and TWO verdict changes when it last estimated -- both CORRECT\nremovals. Converting 40 walks into findings and verdicts is the missing step,\nand it is cheap: the ceiling instrument already has both arms.\n\nTHE SAFETY TRADE THE OWNER NOW OWNS, quoted from this item because unparking is\nwhen it becomes live: \"without alias analysis (excluded by ADR-0017 section 7b)\nthis introduces FALSE NEGATIVES on container/alias mutation. For a security\ntool that is the expensive direction.\" Refutation REMOVES findings. Building\nsection 7a to enable it means a repo can go from violated to clean because the\ntool decided a flow is not real. That is the direction that fails silently.\n\nAND ONE RANKING FACT NEITHER ITEM CARRIED: WI-kabif now gates TWO independent\nfamilies -- the escape-closing family (INV-busis, INV-mumov, INV-linub,\nINV-foluz), and java's def/use extractor (WI-gotun), whose section 3a\nrefutation payoff is gated the same way. That is why P1 rather than P2."  # 8989
- op: discuss  # 2d25
  at: '2026-08-25T23:28:18Z'  # 2d25
  by: agent  # 2d25
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2d25
  clock: 10  # 2d25
  nonce: 2d25  # 2d25
  message: "REFUTATION PRICED IN FINDINGS AND VERDICTS 2026-08-25, at the owner's\ninstruction. New instrument: p4_busis_08252026/measure-refutation-payoff.py.\nRaw: json/refutation.json.\n\nTHE QUESTION THE CEILING RUN COULD NOT ANSWER. Section 3a tests\n`_ddg_taint_reaches(...) is True`, so closing escapes (None -> False) cannot\nmove it -- that zero was a tautology. This arm grants the walk the REMOVAL\nAUTHORITY WI-kabif proposes: a False DROPS the flow.\n\n  ARM A  production control.\n  ARM C  every escape forced closed AND a section 3a False drops the finding.\n\nATTRIBUTION IS 1:1 BY CONSTRUCTION, not by a fuzzy join. The section 3a walk is\ninvoked at exactly one site in propagate_taint_ddg and the single\nfindings.append() for that iteration follows it, with only the barrier arm in\nbetween (excluded by checking barrier_lines). The walk's verdict is held\npending and tags the next finding constructed, then resets.\n\nCONTROL FIRED ON ALL FOUR REPOS -- arm C demonstrably removed findings, which\nis the precondition the ceiling run lacked.\n\n  repo           findings made   refuted   evidence A -> C   violated\n  pretix                   926         9        99 -> 98        6 -> 6\n  caddy                    749        22        16 -> 14        6 -> 6\n  alertmanager             207         2         4 ->  4        4 -> 4\n  kserve                   180         7        71 -> 68        4 -> 4\n  TOTAL                  2,062        40       190 -> 184      20 -> 20\n\n  findings refuted : 40 of 2,062 constructed (1.9%)\n  evidence records : -6 (-3.2%)\n  VERDICT CHANGES  : ZERO. No claim flips out of violated on any repo.\n\nCROSS-INSTRUMENT RECONCILIATION, which is the strongest check here: the 40\nfindings refuted equals EXACTLY the 40 refutable walks the independent ceiling\nrun measured (9/22/2/7 per repo, matching repo for repo). And caddy's 16\nevidence records match measurement 0005's 16 situations for caddy exactly, so\nthis instrument is reading the same population 0005 adjudicated.\n\nWHY 40 DROPPED FINDINGS REMOVE ONLY 6 RECORDS, and this is the load-bearing\nmechanism: 34 of the 40 shared a collapsed SITUATION with a finding that\nsurvived (INV-karud). The record stays and its collapsed_flow_count shrinks, so\nthe reader sees no change. Refutation deletes rows inside situations rather\nthan deleting situations.\n\nSO THE THREE OPTIONS ON THIS ITEM NOW ALL CARRY NUMBERS:\n  1. narrow refutation's domain    ZERO walks refutable (measured, PR #197)\n  2. build section 7a              -3.2% evidence, ZERO verdicts -- AT THE\n                                   CEILING, i.e. assuming every escape closes\n  3. retire the removal goal       zero, deliberately\n\nOption 2 is the only one that buys anything, and what it buys is invisible at\nthe level a user acts on. Real section 7a would close some escapes, not all,\nso the achievable figure is strictly below -3.2% / 0 verdicts.\n\nAGAINST THIS ITEM'S OWN PRE-REGISTRATION, which said to suspect a much LARGER\nnumber: predicted ~13% fewer rows, previously measured -10.3% on the UNGUARDED\narm with 2 verdict changes. Today: -3.2% and 0. Smaller, and the direction is\nexplained -- the two soundness guards (source_tracked, sink_after_source), both\nadded after verified false negatives, restrict when the walk runs at all. The\nearlier figure was measured without them. No alarm is warranted by the\npre-registration's own rule.\n\nTHE TRADE, RESTATED AGAINST THE NUMBER: buying -3.2% of evidence rows and zero\nverdict changes requires building section 7a field-sensitivity -- a capability\nADR-0017 section 7b deliberately excludes -- and introduces FALSE NEGATIVES on\ncontainer/alias mutation into a security tool. That is a large build and a\nsilent failure direction, purchased with a change no user of the verdict would\nobserve.\n\nLIMITS, stated rather than implied:\n  * FOUR REPOS, and caddy is one of them -- the exact concentration defect\n    INV-duvup is being built to fix. These four are not a frame cohort.\n  * Evidence denominators are wildly uneven (caddy 16, pretix 99, kserve 71),\n    so the pooled -3.2% is a pooled census, the estimator INV-duvup rejects.\n  * SINGLE PASS BY ONE AGENT. 0005's lesson was that a blind pass agreeing\n    0/37 was still not enough. The cross-instrument reconciliation above is a\n    real check; independent adjudication of the 40 refutals is not done."  # 2d25
