  message: "ADJUDICATION OF THE 40 REMOVALS -- PRE-REGISTERED 2026-08-25 19:40:45, before any of the 40 was looked at. Full text: p4_busis_08252026/ADJUDICATION-PREREGISTRATION.md.\n\nQUESTION: for each finding refutation removed, was the REMOVAL CORRECT (the finding was a FALSE POSITIVE) or INCORRECT (it was a TRUE POSITIVE, i.e. refutation deleted a real flow -- a false negative, the expensive direction)?\n\nRUBRIC: 0001's, cited verbatim per frame F6, not rewritten. TP = the source value or a data-flow derivative is an ARGUMENT or RECEIVER of the sink call, with citable lines. FP = any link absent, including co-location, call-graph reachability with no value passed, and control-dependence-only. UNADJUDICABLE counted beside, never folded in. Tie-break: taint flows through IN-PROGRAM COMPUTATION, not through an external resource selected by the tainted value.\n\nTHIS ARM HAS A NAMED REASON TO PRODUCE INCORRECT REMOVALS, recorded before the result so it cannot be invoked afterwards to explain away a bad number. The ceiling forces _use_site_terminates -> True at EVERY use site, asserting 'the callee consumed and discarded this value'. True for fmt.Printf(cwd); FALSE for lst.append(x) (escapes into the receiver) and y = f(x) (propagates to the return). So a False verdict here can rest on a MANUFACTURED termination.\n\nTHE ASYMMETRY THAT FOLLOWS, and it bounds what this adjudication can conclude: these removals should be MORE error-prone than a real section 7a implementation's, because real field-sensitivity TRACKS the value instead of asserting it died. So a HIGH incorrect-removal rate here does not by itself condemn section 7a; a LOW one is strong evidence in its favour.\n\nPREDICTIONS, so they can be scored:\n  1. Most removals correct -- 0005 put precision at 21.6%/situation and 10.0%/row on an overlapping cohort, so most findings here are false positives already.\n  2. INCORRECT REMOVALS: 0 to 8 of 40 (0-20%), central estimate 4 (10%). Below the TP base rate, because the walk removes where it found no dependence.\n  3. Incorrect ones CLUSTER on uses where the forced termination does the work -- container appends, assignments read later -- rather than spreading uniformly.\n  4. UNADJUDICABLE non-trivial: intraprocedural so the code is readable, but Go 'external' receivers and Django dynamic attribute access recur here.\n\nIf the result lands far outside 0-20%, suspect the instrument before believing it."  # c3fb
- op: discuss  # 7771
  at: '2026-08-25T23:46:59Z'  # 7771
  by: agent  # 7771
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7771
  clock: 12  # 7771
  nonce: '7771'  # 7771
  message: "ADJUDICATION OF THE 40 REMOVALS -- COMPLETE 2026-08-25. Every one read in\nsource against 0001's rubric. Detail: p4_busis_08252026/json/refuted-40.json.\n\nRESULT: 33 CORRECT (82.5%), 7 INCORRECT (17.5%), 0 unadjudicable.\n\nPre-registered 0-8 incorrect with a central estimate of 4. Measured 7 -- inside\nthe band, at the upper end. Prediction 3 said the incorrect ones would CLUSTER\non container appends and assignments read later rather than spreading\nuniformly. ALL SEVEN fit that pattern; none is a counterexample.\n\nTHE 7 INCORRECT REMOVALS -- real flows refutation deleted:\n\n  #4 pretix vouchers_send   vouchers = Voucher.objects.filter(...)   [33]\n     voucher_list.append(vouchers.pop(0))                            [38]\n     v.tag/v.comment mutated                                      [52-56]\n     Voucher.objects.bulk_update(voucher_list, fields=['comment','tag'])  [68]\n     The sink WRITES the mutated fields. Unambiguous.\n  #5 pretix vouchers_send   same source -> logs (via a comprehension binding\n     at 41 and log_action at 57) -> LogEntry.objects.bulk_create(logs)  [69]\n  #7 pretix vouchers_send   user = User.objects.get(pk=user)         [34]\n     -> log_action(user=user) [59] -> logs -> bulk_create             [69]\n  #1 pretix build_invoice   rate = ExchangeRate.objects.filter(...)\n     -> invoice.foreign_currency_rate = rate.rate.quantize(...)      [204]\n     -> InvoiceLine.objects.create(invoice=invoice, ...)             [290]\n     BORDERLINE and flagged: the sink writes an InvoiceLine, and the tainted\n     field lives on the Invoice written by a DIFFERENT call (invoice.save()\n     at 213). Counted TP on 0001's own container precedent (the pretix\n     buffer/reportlab tie-break). Strict count without it is 6 of 40 (15%).\n  #35 kserve kservedeployer  output_path = args.output_path          [449]\n      -> open(output_path, \"w\")                                      [560]\n  #36 kserve validate-install-scripts  for path_str in args.paths    [365]\n      -> path = Path(path_str) -> print(f\"...{path}\", file=sys.stderr)[368]\n      Loop-variable binding, named explicitly in the rubric.\n  #39 kserve pip-licenses    license_path = os.path.join(args.output_path,\n      \"LICENSE.txt\") [356] -> open(license_path, \"w\")                 [360]\n\nCROSS-CHECK AGAINST A PRIOR INDEPENDENT ADJUDICATION: #23 (caddy\nListenPacket -> Chmod, where `address` is an INPUT to the source rather than\nits output) I labelled a CORRECT removal. WI-kabif's own earlier history\nlabelled that same case a correct removal, independently. The two agree.\n\nNOTABLE CORRECT REMOVALS, i.e. genuine false positives refutation catches:\n  * SCOPE CONFUSION (#17, #18): cmdFmt's stdin `input` [682] lives inside\n    `if configFile == \"-\"` and RETURNS at 688. The sink at 700 consumes a\n    DIFFERENT `input` from os.ReadFile at 691. The tool conflated two\n    same-named variables in disjoint scopes.\n  * LITERAL-ARGUMENT SINKS (#11, #14, #15, #20, #21, #22, #24, #25, #26):\n    fmt.Print(\"\\nModule versions:\\n\\n\"), fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr) -- the sink's\n    argument is a string literal or empty.\n  * SINK BEFORE SOURCE (#8, #33): the recorded sink line precedes the source.\n  * CONTROL DEPENDENCE ONLY (#27, #28): isWindows := runtime.GOOS == \"windows\"\n    guards the branch; the sink's argument is a literal filename.\n  * FILE-CONTENT TIE-BREAK (#2, #3): cf is a DB row whose .file is parsed, so\n    the data comes from the filesystem -- 0001's mitmproxy precedent.\n\nTHE PRE-REGISTERED CAVEAT NOW BINDS, and it cuts in refutation's favour. Every\none of the 7 errors is attributable to the CEILING'S FIAT rather than to\nrefutation as such: forcing _use_site_terminates -> True asserts the value died\nat `voucher_list.append(...)`, at `logs.append(...)`, at\n`invoice.foreign_currency_rate = ...`. A REAL section 7a implementation tracks\ncontainers and fields instead of asserting termination, so it would get exactly\nthese cases right. THIS ERROR RATE IS AN UPPER BOUND AND PROBABLY A LARGE\nOVERESTIMATE. I cannot conclude real refutation errs at 17.5%.\n\nSO THE DESIGN CALL DOES NOT TURN ON THE ERROR RATE. It turns on the payoff,\nwhich is unchanged by this adjudication: at the absolute ceiling, refutation\nremoves 33 genuine false positives, and that is worth -6 evidence records\n(-3.2%) and ZERO verdict changes across four repositories. Even granting a\nperfect implementation with zero errors, nothing a user reads changes.\n\nWHAT WOULD CHANGE THE ANSWER: a claim whose ENTIRE evidence set is false\npositives, where removal flips violated -> confirmed. Zero of 20 violated\nclaims did that here. The 33 correct removals were spread across claims that\nretained other evidence, which is the same collapse arithmetic that made 40\ndropped findings cost only 6 records."  # 7771
- op: discuss  # e070
  at: '2026-08-26T06:29:10Z'  # e070
  by: agent  # e070
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e070
  clock: 13  # e070
  nonce: e070  # e070
  message: "RE-PRICED ON REAL DATA (INV-zidur unblocked it; docs/measurements/0007).\n\nTHE +6.3 POINTS WAS NOT AN UPPER BOUND IN NEED OF REFINEMENT -- IT WAS PRICED ON\nTHE WRONG FIELD. Of 153 ddg_mixed evidence rows over 11 repositories, the number\nthat rest on a walk which ran and established no dependence is ZERO -- in every\nrepository, not merely in aggregate. 90.8% rest on a walk that NEVER RAN and\n9.2% on a walk that ran and LOST TRACK. Every removal section 7a would authorise\nunder \"drop every ddg_mixed\" is removal-on-ignorance.\n\nYOUR OWN TRIPWIRE IS WHAT FOUND THIS. The filing says: \"Addressable domain is\ntherefore about 18 percent of flows. If a future measurement reports a much\nlarger number, suspect the measurement.\" It reported 26.8%. Suspecting the\nmeasurement is the whole of this result.\n\nWHY THE WALK DOES NOT RUN, measured rather than assumed (first guard, over the\n139 not_attempted rows; these PARTITION the population, so a remedy for the top\nblocker promotes flows to the NEXT one rather than to the walk):\n\n  cross_function       106   76.3%\n  source_not_tracked    24   17.3%\n  sink_before_source     9    6.5%\n\nThis filing predicted the top row in advance from a DIFFERENT cohort -- \"69\npercent of flows have source and sink in different functions, which\nintraprocedural DDG cannot connect by construction\" -- and 76.3% is that number\nmeasured a second way. sink_before_source at 6.5% is a FLOOR, not a bound:\nWI-pohib already records that the test is lexical, so a sink in a closure that\nexecutes later reads as sink-first.\n\nTHE DESIGN CALL -- build section 7a or retire it -- IS ANSWERED NEITHER.\nIt is blocked on SECTION 4 FUNCTION SUMMARIES, which is blocker 5 in this item's\nown discussion, not on labelling and not on the removal rule. Building the\nremoval arm now would authorise removals with an evidence-backed domain of zero;\nretiring it would discard an arm whose domain is unmeasured because the walk\ncannot yet reach the flows, not because the flows resist it.\n\nWHAT WOULD MOVE THE NUMBER, in order: section 4 summaries (76.3% of the blocked\npopulation), receiver/def tracking at the source (17.3%), INV-busis escape-site\nclosure (the 14 escaped rows -- 9.2% of ddg_mixed, 4.7% of all rows, the ONLY\npopulation where closing escapes could produce an unconfirmed).\n\nITEM STAYS todo_hard. The blocker is now NAMED AND SIZED rather than suspected."  # e070
- op: discuss  # 002a
  at: '2026-08-26T16:26:03Z'  # 002a
  by: agent  # 002a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 002a
  clock: 14  # 002a
  nonce: 002a  # 002a
  message: "YOUR DESIGN CALL IS NOW PRICED FROM THE OTHER SIDE (measurement 0008, WI-famig).\nNO STATUS CHANGE -- the owner's instruction 2026-08-26 is that build-or-retire\nwill be revisited later, so this records evidence only.\n\nI TOLD THIS ITEM, ON 2026-08-26, THAT IT WAS \"BLOCKED ON SECTION 4 FUNCTION\nSUMMARIES\". THAT WAS IMPRECISE IN A WAY THAT MATTERED, and correcting it is most\nof this note. Section 4 is TWO halves:\n  * 4b DECLARED summaries: LIVE since #197. load_function_summaries() is called\n    at taint.py:3363 and its terminating entries feed _use_site_terminates. This\n    is why this item's own tally records blocker 5 as DONE -- and that record is\n    correct.\n  * 4a INFERRED summaries: zero production callers, and the shipped\n    FunctionSummary omits param_to_calls / param_to_param / symbol_id entirely\n    (repo-wide grep: those three appear ONLY in the ADR text). param_to_calls is\n    the field a cross-function walk needs. Filed as WI-famig.\nSo the blocker is 4a-plus-composition, not \"section 4\".\n\nAND THE PRICING SAYS 4a DOES NOT UNBLOCK YOUR REMOVAL ARM.\n\nThe chain removal authority depends on is: cross_function -> (4a composition) ->\nwalk RUNS -> returns UNCONFIRMED -> (7a) removal -> dropped finding -> (collapse)\n-> maybe a row. Four gates in series. The measurement kills it at gate three:\n\n  Of the 28 walks that RAN across the 11 repositories:\n      14 confirmed / 14 escaped / ZERO unconfirmed.\n\n`unconfirmed` is the ONLY class removal can act on, and it is 0 -- in every\nrepository, and reproduced independently in 0007. Composition manufactures\nRUNNING walks; on the observed split those are confirmations and escapes.\nNothing in 4a creates the class you need.\n\nTHE CEILING, for completeness: 18.3% of cross-function findings (778 of 4,245)\nmeet the necessary conditions for a single-hop composed walk; per-repo median\n22.3%, range 0-100%. That is the size of what composition could REACH, not of\nwhat it would REFUTE.\n\nA CONSEQUENCE FOR THIS ITEM'S OWN ARITHMETIC THAT WAS NOT PREVIOUSLY NAMED.\nYour 2026-08-25 note explains that 40 dropped findings cost only 6 evidence\nrecords because 34 shared a collapsed situation with a survivor. The mechanism\nis asymmetric and the other direction is worse for you: analysis_method is IN\nthe collapse key and ADJUDICATED FLOWS BYPASS COLLAPSE ENTIRELY\n(taint.py:641, UNADJUDICATED_METHODS = {structural, ddg_mixed}). So\n  * a REFUTED finding removes a row only if EVERY member of its situation goes;\n  * a CONFIRMED finding becomes ITS OWN ROW, and the ddg_mixed group it left\n    survives one member lighter.\nRefutation is throttled by collapse; confirmation is AMPLIFIED by it. At the\ncomposition ceiling that is up to 778 new `precise` rows on a cohort emitting\n298 rows in total.\n\nWHAT WOULD CHANGE THE ANSWER, stated so it is not mistaken for closed: the\n0-of-28 unconfirmed rate is a SMALL DENOMINATOR. It is consistent across every\nrepository and across 0007's independent run, but \"unconfirmed is 0 among walks\nthat run TODAY\" is not the same proposition as \"unconfirmed would be ~0 among\nwalks composition MAKES run\". That inference is load-bearing and it is NOT\nmeasured. If 4a is ever built, that is the first number to take."  # 002a
- op: discuss  # a909
  at: '2026-09-02T12:08:33Z'  # a909
  by: agent  # a909
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a909
  clock: 15  # a909
  nonce: a909  # a909
  message: "PREREQUISITE ADDED: WI-vosug, and it comes from work that shipped rather than from re-reading this thread.\n\nINV-foluz shipped in PR #711 (dev a33de088bc). It fixes the largest single cause of section 3a escapes — a bare-name call emitting no edge at all — and in doing so it CHANGES THE SUBSTRATE THIS ITEM WOULD BE EXERCISED ON, in the direction that makes this item weaker.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, read in code rather than inferred. taint.py's call_beside_heir branch enumerates PERMITTING cases:\n    if not (callees_at or {}).get((symbol_id, use_line)): continue   # no callee   -> NOT an escape\n    if _use_site_terminates(...):                          continue   # terminates -> NOT an escape\n    escaped = True                                                    # callee, no summary -> ESCAPE\nSo a callee reaching callees_at WITHOUT a section 4 summary converts 'not an escape' into an escape. Before #711 those bare builtin calls were invisible and took the first branch; now they take the third.\n\nMEASURED. #711 adds 13,193 edges on hypergumbo-core and 8,359 on pretix (0 lost). python_stdlib.yaml holds exactly ONE builtin FUNCTION summary — builtins.print — so 459 of the 13,193 are consultable and 12,734 are not.\n\nDIRECTION, PRECISELY, because it is not all bad. A confirmation cannot be lost: return True short-circuits at taint.py:3598, before the post-loop 'if escaped: return None' at :3690. The movement is False -> None ONLY — strictly fewer refutations, never a suppressed finding. Under today's confirm-only section 3a that is inert (the arm tests 'is True', so False and None collapse). Under THIS item it is not inert: it is exactly the verdict this item exists to license.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR SEQUENCING, offered as measured input and not as a decision. The owner granted removal authority on 2026-09-02. That ruling stands. But the pre-registered expectation recorded in this item's own filing — roughly 13% fewer evidence rows, ZERO of 17 violated claim verdicts changing — was priced against the PRE-#711 substrate, and the escape population has moved since. Either WI-vosug lands first, or this item should re-derive its expectation before acting on the old one. Do not read a smaller-than-expected removal count after #711 as this item failing."  # a909
