- op: discuss  # 6dc2
  at: '2026-09-02T19:49:06Z'  # 6dc2
  by: agent  # 6dc2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6dc2
  clock: 17  # 6dc2
  nonce: 6dc2  # 6dc2
  message: "DONE, PR #716 (merged, dev b26d97bd11). The headline this item was filed on --\n\"make the DDG forward walk decide flow inclusion\" -- is met in the only\ndirection the walk can honestly claim: it SUBTRACTS. A flow whose walk returns\n`unconfirmed` is removed; the walk still mints nothing, so inclusion remains\nbounded by call-graph reachability.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (production path, propagate_taint_ddg): a fixture reaching\nwalk_verdict == \"unconfirmed\" yields 0 findings where it previously yielded 1,\nwith a non-vacuity floor (add one DDG edge so the value DOES reach the sink ->\n1 finding, walk_verdict \"confirmed\"), escaped/not_attempted controls that keep\ntheir flows, and the WI-joluk gate test with a vacuity guard. 11 tests.\n\n*** THE PRE-REGISTERED EXPECTATION CANNOT BE SCORED, AND SAYING SO IS THE\nHONEST OUTCOME. *** This item pre-registered \"roughly 13 percent fewer evidence\nrows and ZERO of 17 violated claim verdicts change\", and warned: \"If a future\nmeasurement reports a much larger number, suspect the measurement.\" The measured\nnumber is not larger. It is ZERO, and for a reason the filing did not anticipate:\n\n    hypergumbo-core, scripts/measure-taint-arm-census.py at dev 54edacb18c\n      ('s3a', False, 'True') -> 14      ('s3a', True, 'True') ->  1\n      ('s3a', False, 'None') ->  8      ('s3a', True, 'None') ->  4\n      TOTAL 27 walks, ZERO returning False\n\n    11-repo cohort, ddg_mixed rows: 0 unconfirmed / 14 escaped / 139 not_attempted\n\n`unconfirmed` is the ONLY class removal can act on and it is EMPTY. So this\nships live semantics over an empty class. It is not inert by accident and it is\nnot a no-op that should have been left unbuilt: the semantics are what make\nevery escape-closing item worth anything, and the ordering is forced -- WI-joluk\nrequired the grant to land in the same PR as the gate.\n\n*** WHY THE CLASS IS EMPTY, AND WHAT WOULD FILL IT. *** Escapes, not\ncross-function bails. scripts/measure-escape-closing-ceiling.py forces\n_use_site_terminates to True for every site:\n\n    section 3a walks T/F/None   control 15/0/12   ceiling 15/7/5\n    FINDINGS violated/sanitized/evidence   5/0/11 in BOTH arms\n\nClosing every escape converts 7 escapes into refutations. That is a CEILING and\nnot a prediction -- the ceiling arm also closes callees that genuinely\npropagate, so the correct subset is smaller and unknown. The remaining escape\nsites on the self-tree have named owners: INV-mumov 1, INV-linub 3, WI-zumud 2\n(correctly provenance-gated), plus one honest propagation. INV-linub is the\nbiggest single block.\n\nRE-REGISTERED, so the old number is not silently inherited: the ~13% row\nreduction belongs to the ESCAPE-CLOSURE work (INV-linub, INV-mumov), not to this\ngrant. Anyone measuring after those land should compare against 0, not against\n13%.\n\n*** WHAT I DID NOT INHERIT FROM THIS THREAD, HAVING CHECKED IT. *** The\n2026-08-xx note concluding \"AND THE PRICING SAYS 4a DOES NOT UNBLOCK YOUR\nREMOVAL ARM ... 14 confirmed / 14 escaped / ZERO unconfirmed\" is REPRODUCED here\non a different corpus and instrument. Its conclusion about section 4a\ncomposition is untouched by this PR; what changed is only that the arm now acts\non the class when it is non-empty.\n\n*** THE TRADE, RECORDED WHERE THE ITEM FILED IT. *** This item's \"KNOWN TRADE TO\nOWN IN WRITING\" -- false negatives on container/alias mutation, since ADR-0017\nsection 7b excludes alias analysis -- is now live. Section 7b additionally states\na preference for overapproximation over underapproximation, so the grant is a\ndeliberate departure from the ADR's own stated default; the owner made it\nexplicitly on 2026-09-02 and the code comment says so rather than presenting the\nremoval as ADR-mandated.\n\n*** ONE THING THIS PR ADDED THAT THE FILING DID NOT ASK FOR. *** A removal that\nnobody can count is a security tool silently reporting fewer findings than its\nanalysis produced. verify-claims now publishes\ndataflow_coverage.flows_removed_by_walk on the JSON and text surfaces, separate\nfrom findings_total (survivors). First live run: 0.\n\nRESIDUAL, NOT CLOSED BY THIS. WI-gotun (java has 69 sinks, a CFG mapping and NO\ndef/use extractor, so it contributes zero DDG edges) was grouped into this phase\nby the campaign plan. It is additive, carries no removal risk, and is NOT in\nthis PR -- bundling a new extractor with a semantics change would have made both\nharder to review. It stays open."  # 6dc2
